 would reboot a property the  first reason would be if the current  series that you've got is simply too  tainted this is kind of the Batman of  Robins scenario now that film left such  a bad taste in everybody's mouth that  really the only way to move forward with  bad  on film was to wipe that away and start  from scratch now as much as I personally  may not care what the second  Ghostbusters film I don't think that's  the case here and I don't think you can  argue that it is there's still a very  great and very strong love for these  characters I mean that's why this movies  happening at all now another reason to  reboot a franchise is the age of the  actors and this would think of say the  Star Trek reboot that was a case the  actors where they were too old to keep  going the only way to move forward is to  start over and get young people to  embody these characters so that you can  basically restart the timeline again  again that's also really not the case  here I mean up until Harold Ramis dying  this was going to be a sequel now yes I  understand he's dead and the actors are  older but just look at the fact that  we're not actually dealing with the same  characters we're dealing with the same  concept on a whole new set of characters  now it may actually turn out that each  of these female characters is an analog  for one of the pre-existing male  ghostbusters but even if that is the  case of just rebuilding off the  archetype they're not really rebooting  the characters and doing that sort of  younger reboot for our characters is  really only necessary if the characters  themselves are absolutely intrinsic to  the central concept and it cannot move  forward without those same characters  and again obviously that's not the case  we have a whole new set of characters  here another reason to reboot a  franchise is if you want to take it in a  direction that the existing material  simply does not allow you to go in maybe  you've got new ideas that just  inherently go against the Canon of  established film so far maybe the tone  is just not is not in keeping with what  has happened before this will kind of be  like the Casino Royale example I mean  James Bond had been recast several times  up to that point and none of those have  really been a reboot but this was a case  where they wanted to go back tell a  story of his first mission but not have  it be a period be set in the 60s so that  was the reason for that reboot what they  wanted to do could not be done with the  existing timeline a story that had been  established now while we don't really  know all the ins and outs of the story  that's gonna be told in this new  Ghostbusters everything that's been  talked about with the people behind it  has been very emphatically saying that  the tone is going to be the same as in  the previous film so again no need for a  reboot there finally the last  reason to reboot is when a film is an  adaptation of an existing property that  you can make the argument that the  reboot is being truer to the source  material or maybe is gonna emphasize  aspect of the source material that were  not done in the previous adaptation  again James Bond kind of falls under  this a little bit but again that does  not apply to ghostbusters because this  was a film first this was not an  adaptation of existing material there's  been a franchise worth of material since  then but it was always a film first now  coming back to what I said before about  the fact that we don't know a ton about  this story but even with as little as we  know I don't feel that having an entire  new team of ghostbusters is enough to  justify a reboot unto itself I mean why  can't they just be the next generation  of ghostbusters why can't they just be a  separate franchise of ghostbusters I  mean Dan Aykroyd's original concept of  the thing was actually that they would  be very much like firemen and there will  be fire stations and new stations of  ghostbusters all over the city all over  the country so why can't this just be a  different group hey you can even keep  the fact that they're gonna make their  own gear it got established and  ghostbusters 2 that supernatural  activity waxes and wanes I mean at the  start of ghostbusters 2 things have been  completely quiet to the point that the  Ghostbusters basically had been out of  business for the past few years now I  actually don't think that was a  particularly good idea story wise in  ghostbusters 2 but now that that already  has been established it's not perfectly  reasonable that the original  Ghostbusters would have retired and that  this is a new group coming up and maybe  this new group is making their own stuff  they're on proton packs and so forth  based off of maybe older broken-down  models are just what they understand the  original Ghostbusters were using and  that idea what actually even worked  really well with the shots that we've  seen that have been released of the  proton packs and of ecto-1 and so forth  it's all very much strongly the  aesthetic of the original films but it's  not quite exactly that I mean really it  looks like what someone who maybe had a  blueprint of a proton pack but not the  actual thing itself would have put  together and if they were doing this  instead of rebooting the use of the  exact same logo would actually  makes sense because they just be repro  creating it for this new generation of  this new franchise of ghostbusters  as opposed to having it be a completely  different continuity but they just  coincidentally happen to use the exact  same logo  I'm pretty sure they're even bringing  back Slimer whose iconic as heck but is  in no way vital to the storytelling  there's all this emphasis whenever the  director talks and whenever they release  these publicity stills that look see  it's just like you remembered but if  it's just like I remember why are you  rebooting it why are we ignoring all the  stuff that came before  generally the point of a reboot as I've  laid out is to go it with a new  direction do something different but  you're not you're emphasizing how much  it's the same look the only way that I  can think of that the story might demand  that this thing be rebooted is it there  completely restructuring the rules and  the way that ghosts and the technology  function but I honestly can't even bring  myself to believe that that's gonna be  the case because the rules were so  loosely defined in the first place that  if you just overlaid the correct techno  jargon over it you can do anything you  want  look I am just really infuriated that  it's a reboot and they're getting rid of  the old stuff because there's nothing  that I have seen about any aspect of  this that justifies throwing out the old  continuity in fact I find myself keep  thinking if they were keeping the old  stuff it would save a whole bunch of  time now instead they're gonna have to  dedicate screen time to explaining the  ghosts the traps the proton packs when  by all indications they're not doing  anything new or different with any of  those things again let me stress I don't  care that it's a new team I love the old  team but I don't need them to be enemies  even before Harold Ramis died I didn't  need to see them old running around  chasing ghosts I mean Indiana Jones for  kind of proved to me that that's not a  good idea I don't care that it's a team  of women and just having a new team it  doesn't require anything in terms of  race or gender you can go any direction  with it I don't care that Chris  Hemsworth is the secretary Hey  I heard that that was the first bit of  news about this movie that actually kind  of made me smile because I thought  that's kind of funny as a concept I  don't need the exact version of  ghostbusters that I grew up with to be  put up on skirt on screen for my own  nostalgic purposes I honestly would  rather it would just leave the franchise  alone all together but what I really  haven't heard is a single reason for why  my version and my film that I love  shouldn't count anymore I haven't heard  the argument I know that the old movie  doesn't suddenly go away and it doesn't  exist but it's still kind of sweeping it  under the rug going yeah we're not gonna  talk about that anymore  and I could deal with that and I would  not be so frustrated and so exasperated  if somebody anybody give me a reason a  necessary reason why this is a reboot  and not a continuation cuz I haven't  heard it and until I hear it I can't  possibly get excited about a new  Ghostbusters so that's it that's my  argument do you think there is a reason  to be rebooting this instead of having  it just be continuation with a new team  if you do believe there was a reason  please share something down in the  comments and let's talk about it but  until next time this council is  adjourned

